  "description": "<p>Contra Costa College has been a proud Hispanic-serving institution, serving mostly Latinx, African American and Asian students since 1949. It is located in San Pablo, California, and is the oldest of the three colleges in the Contra Costa Community College District.</p><p>O 7,000 students enrol each year, and over 60 countries are represented. Students can choose from more than 127 degree and certificate options in various interests and disciplines.</p><h2>What is the Contra Costa College acceptance rate for International Students?</h2><p>The acceptance rate is 100% for Contra Costa College.</p> <p>Contra Costa College boasts many facilities to support students' overall college experience. The campus offers ergonomically designed classrooms equipped with modern technology and well-equipped laboratories. The college also houses a comprehensive learning centre with tutoring services, workshops, and academic support to assist students in reaching their educational goals. In addition, Contra Costa College has art studios, music practice rooms, and theatre facilities to allow for better creative expression. The campus provides a fitness centre, sports fields, and a swimming pool so students can maintain an active and healthy lifestyle.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>The Associated Student Union of Contra Costa College (ASUCCC) has 20 active members and represents students in various matters. The diversity of the students is visible in the range of events held throughout the year and the multiculturalism in the student body. Student ambassadors welcome students into the community and help to facilitate community outreach resource programs.</p>",
